sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Student
    actor A as Admin
    actor V as Anyone (employer)
    participant CE as certificate-service
    participant AD as admission
    participant AS as assessment
    participant BA as batch
    participant CR as course
    participant FI as finance
    participant ID as identity
    participant K as Kafka

    S->>CE: GET /api/certificates/eligibility
    CE->>CR: completion rule for the course
    CE->>BA: attendance %, enrolment (taken from the student's own enrolment)
    CE->>AS: required tests passed?
    CE->>FI: fees settled?
    CE-->>S: checklist: each condition met or not (unreachable = not met)

    S->>CE: POST /api/certificates/requests
    CE->>CE: request PENDING
    CE->>K: notification.requested (staff told)

    A->>CE: approve or reject (reason)
    alt approved
        CE->>CE: APPROVED
        A->>CE: POST /requests/{id}/issue
        CE->>CE: re-check every condition at the moment of issue
        CE->>ID: institute branding and signatory
        CE->>CE: certificate number + verification code, PDF
        CE->>CE: request ISSUED
        CE->>K: certificate.issued
        CE->>K: notification.requested (student)
    else rejected
        CE->>CE: REJECTED
        CE->>K: notification.requested (student)
    end

    S->>CE: GET /api/certificates/{id}/pdf
    V->>CE: GET /api/certificates/verify/{number} (public, 1/s per address)
    CE-->>V: valid, name, course, date, or revoked
    A->>CE: POST /api/certificates/{id}/revoke (ADMIN only)
